.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt ASA 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm asa
.Nd interpret FORTRAN carriage-control characters
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads each
.Ar file
in order, or the standard input when no file is given or a file is
.Ql - ,
and writes the text with the first character of every line interpreted as
a FORTRAN carriage-control character:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It space
Advance one line.
Any character other than the controls below is treated
as a space.
.It Ql 0
Advance two lines.
.It Ql 1
Advance to the first line of the next page (form feed).
.It Ql +
Overstrike the previous line (carriage return).
.El
.Pp
The control character is removed from the output.
The first line of a file
does not start with a blank line or carriage return.
A non-empty input ends
with a newline.
.Pp
The target image reads the standard input from the console.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cal 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the POSIX asa carriage-control subset for the C locale.
